+ * it read 64 KB to get its 30-byte header (libnix's buffer is 64 KB; a random
+ * seek and a 64 KB read cost 3.1 ms there, a seek and a 64-byte read 0.47 ms:
+ * tests/a1200/io-probe). Here a seek only moves the position; small reads come
+ * from a block read at once, reads of a block or more go straight to the
+ * caller. On AmigaOS the file is read through dos.library (no stdio buffer
+ * in between), without a Seek when a read goes straight on, and the streams
+ * opened on the same file share one handle (the port runs in one task; each
+ * read seeks for itself): a new stream costs no Open (0.3 ms). Streams opened
+ * for writing pass through to stdio unchanged.
